<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee cooperatives report milder night.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee cooperatives report milder night.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Key Brazilian coffee regions had a milder night, although temperatures in the coldest areas were only marginally higher than on Tuesday, cooperatives and weather stations said early on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The country's coffee regions have had very cold weather over the past few days due to a polar air mass that brought frosts to lower-lying areas where coffee is not grown. The air mass is now moving out to sea.</p>
<p>Weather forecasters are expecting temperatures to pick up gradually, with no damaging cold for coffee in sight.</p>
<p>Early morning/minimum temperatures in degrees Celsius were as follows.</p>
<p>						    June 11	     June</p>
<p>10  PARANA, Londrina region			 7		     6-7</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Presidente Prudente	     12		     10</p>
<p> SAO PAULO, Franca				13			8</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Sao Sebastiao do Paraiso   10			8</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Pocos de Caldas (coop)	4		     3.5</p>
<p> MINAS GERAIS, Guaxupe			   8			4</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
